        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the lack of a proper cleanup mechanism in the `panfrost_clk_init` function when an error occurred while retrieving the `bus_clock`. Specifically, if the `bus_clock` retrieval failed, the function did not call `clk_disable_unprepare()`, which could lead to resource leaks and potential instability in the system.

        Commit message:
        drm/panfrost: Fix missing clk_disable_unprepare() on error in
 panfrost_clk_init()

Fix the missing clk_disable_unprepare() before return
from panfrost_clk_init() in the error handling case.

Fixes: b681af0bc1cc ("drm: panfrost: add optional bus_clock")
Reported-by: Hulk Robot <hulkci@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Wei Yongjun <weiyongjun1@huawei.com>
Reviewed-by: Steven Price <steven.price@arm.com>
Signed-off-by: Steven Price <steven.price@arm.com>
Link: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20210608143856.4154766-1-weiyongjun1@huawei.com  

        Patch:

 static int panfrost_clk_init(struct panfrost_device *pfdev)
 {
 	int err;
 	unsigned long rate;

 	pfdev->clock = devm_clk_get(pfdev->dev, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(pfdev->clock)) {
 		dev_err(pfdev->dev, "get clock failed %ld\n", PTR_ERR(pfdev->clock));
 		return PTR_ERR(pfdev->clock);
 	}

 	rate = clk_get_rate(pfdev->clock);
 	dev_info(pfdev->dev, "clock rate = %lu\n", rate);

 	err = clk_prepare_enable(pfdev->clock);
 	if (err)
 		return err;

 	pfdev->bus_clock = devm_clk_get_optional(pfdev->dev, "bus");
 	if (IS_ERR(pfdev->bus_clock)) {
 		dev_err(pfdev->dev, "get bus_clock failed %ld\n",
 			PTR_ERR(pfdev->bus_clock));
-		return PTR_ERR(pfdev->bus_clock);
+		err = PTR_ERR(pfdev->bus_clock);
+		goto disable_clock;
 	}

 	if (pfdev->bus_clock) {
 		rate = clk_get_rate(pfdev->bus_clock);
 		dev_info(pfdev->dev, "bus_clock rate = %lu\n", rate);

 		err = clk_prepare_enable(pfdev->bus_clock);
 		if (err)
 			goto disable_clock;
 	}

 	return 0;

 disable_clock:
 	clk_disable_unprepare(pfdev->clock);

 	return err;
 }



